// TEST: OrbIdx Wreath Mirrored Read (rejects)
// ERROR: BL4003
// WRITES are implemented; READS are not, and this is the seam that separates
// them. The traversal nest only ever visits CANONICAL cells, so filling a
// wreath pool needs no fold. Subscripting one at an arbitrary tuple does: it
// is §5's per-level sort fold (canonOrb), the accumulated character, and the
// zero set at a '-' level -- none of which is emitted in v1. Refused.
//
// This test also pins a DISPATCH hole, not just a missing feature. A depth-2
// OrbIdx record is ONE index slot spanning prod(ri) = 4 raw axes, so W(i,j,k,l)
// presents 4 args against 1 slot: the arity guard in dispatchAppOrIndex is
// false, no arm matches, and the catch-all mints a fresh inference variable and
// returns Ok. Without an explicit refusal the read TYPECHECKS at a type nothing
// later contradicts and reaches codegen as a dense subscript into a flat pool.
// The explicit arm is what makes this an error rather than a wrong address.
let A = [1.0, 2.0, 3.0]
let g = lambda(x, y) where comm(x, y) -> x * y
let S = method_for(A, A) <@> g |> compute
let h = lambda(p, q) where comm(p, q) -> p + q
let W = method_for(S, S) <@> h |> compute
let mirrored = W(1, 0, 0, 0)
// EXPECT: typecheck failure — a wreath pool has no mirrored (non-canonical) read.
